    "First linker refused CONFIG_CODE exceeding64KB by63 bytes. Moved startup ownership/setup work to the far frontend; CONFIG retains tiny adapters and kind/filename dispatch only. No existing bounds/capacity check weakened.",
    "Second extraction failed the existing call-log queue bounds check because metadata and resident PHONE_LOG_STORAGE shared an AUTO segment base. Explicit module IO/metadata groups plus resident-base exclusion checks fixed it before emulation.",
    "Duplicate-load path reviewed before emulation: refused start must not release an existing claim. Returns state1 directly, confirmed by valid probe.",
    "Initial missing-file harness expected only16 output bytes. Parent exit4 also emits its existing generic keyboard-refusal shutdown notice; final harness checks exact16-byte report and exact known suffix rather than ignoring arbitrary output.",
    "Whole normal parent and startup diagnostic differ by probe-only code; normal GET/UI cases bind normal SHA, startup/fault cases bind probe SHA, including explicit patched-CRC diagnostic identities."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Startup-only authenticated parent API: no live child/compiler bridge, live serial loading or complete arena arbitration. No compiler EXEC occurs in these new parent tests.",
